{"owner":"saahilsanganeriya","name":"GraphML-imts","description":"","htmlUrl":"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts","defaultBranch":"main","sha":"d2d5ea2a62f359a274524c4c3c2b636c24ff28f3","language":"Jupyter Notebook","license":null,"fork":null,"docs":{"EDA_SUMMARY.md":"49e3cb851f60","docs/DATA_PREPROCESSING.md":"68a517724b2d","src/models/raindrop/Raindrop/P12data/processed_data/readme.md":"79875cdd200d","src/models/raindrop/Raindrop/README.md":"c0fad62e2acb","src/models/raindrop/raindrop_readme.md":"27292730042e"},"pushedAt":"2026-10-12T03:09:39Z","fetchedAt":"2026-10-14T13:12:32.118Z","readme":{"path":"README.md","html":"<h1 data-anchor=\"graph-ml-for-irregular-icu-time-series\">Graph ML for Irregular ICU Time Series</h1>\n<p>A four-person class project for a Graph Machine Learning course (Fall 2025). It forecasts the next hours of an ICU\npatient's vital signs and lab values from irregular, mostly missing measurements, using graph neural networks and\nother models built for irregular time series.</p>\n<p>In an ICU record every variable runs on its own clock. Heart rate is charted all through a stay, a troponin test only\nwhen a doctor orders one, so 85.7 % of the variable-by-time slots in this dataset are empty\n(<a href=\"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts/blob/main/EDA_SUMMARY.md\"><code>EDA_SUMMARY.md</code></a>). The models here take that sparse record as it is, without filling the gaps\nfirst.</p>\n<p><strong>Data.</strong> PhysioNet/Computing in Cardiology Challenge 2012: 12,000 ICU stays, the first 48 hours of each,\n36 time-series variables plus 5 static descriptors (age, gender, height, ICU type, weight). <strong>Task.</strong> Given the start\nof a stay, predict the values of the 36 time-series variables that come next. The exact target differs per model; see\n<a href=\"#how-to-read-the-numbers\">How to read the numbers</a>.</p>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"results\">Results</h2>\n<p>All numbers are on z-score normalised values and count only values that were actually measured. Every model uses the\nsame 60/20/20 patient split (seed 42) and the same normalisation, both from <code>scripts/preprocess_data.py</code>. Lower RMSE\nand MAE are better; higher R² is better.</p>\n<p><strong>Midterm (November 2025)</strong>, from the two results tables in <a href=\"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts/blob/main/Reports/midterm.tex\"><code>Reports/midterm.tex</code></a>:</p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Model</th>\n<th>Built by</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Val RMSE</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Val MAE</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Val R²</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Test RMSE</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Test MAE</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Test R²</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>RainDrop</td>\n<td>Saahil</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.561</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.365</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.519</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.596</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.368</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.494</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T-PatchGNN</td>\n<td>Nawal</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.663</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.442</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.451</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.666</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.441</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.442</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GRU-D</td>\n<td>Nawal</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.684</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.456</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.440</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.732</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.456</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.410</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>KAFNet</td>\n<td>Luca</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.719</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.482</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.484</td>\n<td align=\"right\">–</td>\n<td align=\"right\">–</td>\n<td align=\"right\">–</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>WaveGNN</td>\n<td>Asal</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.720</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.508</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.366</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.750</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.540</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.335</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>SeFT</td>\n<td>Luca</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.860</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.627</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.261</td>\n<td align=\"right\">–</td>\n<td align=\"right\">–</td>\n<td align=\"right\">–</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<p>The RainDrop row is also in the run's own output: epoch 50 of\n<a href=\"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts/blob/main/results/raindrop/training_history.json\"><code>results/raindrop/training_history.json</code></a> and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts/blob/main/results/raindrop/test_results/test_results.json\"><code>results/raindrop/test_results/test_results.json</code></a> (2,368 test\npatients). KAFNet and SeFT have no test numbers. Latent ODE did not finish: it trained with batch size 1 and was too\nslow for the full dataset (midterm report, \"Computational Challenges\").</p>\n<p><strong>Final notebook runs (December 2025)</strong>: GRU-D and T-PatchGNN after hyperparameter tuning (commit <code>82ee07f</code>), the VAE's\nfinal run (commit <code>420acee</code>), as printed by each notebook's training and test cells. Validation is the last epoch\n(50 for GRU-D and T-PatchGNN, 35 for the VAE).</p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Model</th>\n<th>Built by</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Val RMSE</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Val MAE</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Val R²</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Test RMSE</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Test MAE</th>\n<th align=\"right\">Test R²</th>\n<th>Source</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>T-PatchGNN</td>\n<td>Nawal</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.648</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.422</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.477</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.643</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.422</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.479</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts/blob/main/src/models/T_PatchGNN.ipynb\"><code>src/models/T_PatchGNN.ipynb</code></a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GRU-D</td>\n<td>Nawal</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.684</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.451</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.440</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.724</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.452</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.422</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts/blob/main/src/models/GRU_D.ipynb\"><code>src/models/GRU_D.ipynb</code></a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Generative VAE</td>\n<td>Nawal</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.805</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.544</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.301</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.817</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.549</td>\n<td align=\"right\">0.277</td>\n<td><a href=\"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts/blob/main/src/models/VAE.ipynb\"><code>src/models/VAE.ipynb</code></a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<h3 data-anchor=\"how-to-read-the-numbers\">How to read the numbers</h3>\n<p>The rows share the split and the normalisation, but each model was scored by its own code and the targets are not the\nsame:</p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Model</th>\n<th>Input</th>\n<th>Target</th>\n<th>Scored on</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>RainDrop</td>\n<td>hours 0–24</td>\n<td>hours 24–30</td>\n<td>one mean per patient and variable over hours 24–30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GRU-D</td>\n<td>hours 0–24</td>\n<td>hours 24–30</td>\n<td>every measured value in hours 24–30</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>T-PatchGNN</td>\n<td>first 64 measurement times</td>\n<td>next 12 measurement times</td>\n<td>every measured value</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Generative VAE</td>\n<td>first 20 measurement times</td>\n<td>next 10 measurement times</td>\n<td>every measured value</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>KAFNet, SeFT, WaveGNN</td>\n<td>–</td>\n<td>–</td>\n<td>the code that sets their target is not in this repository</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<p>So the table does not rank the models. The midterm report ranks RainDrop first, but RainDrop is scored on window\nmeans (<code>compute_loss_and_metrics</code> in <code>src/models/raindrop/train_raindrop_forecasting.py</code>), which is a smoother target\nthan the single values the notebook models predict. What the table does show:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>After tuning, T-PatchGNN's test RMSE went from 0.666 to 0.643 and GRU-D's from 0.732 to 0.724.</li>\n<li>The midterm report sees two patterns across models (\"Common Patterns\"): variables measured often (heart rate,\nblood pressure) are forecast better than sparse labs (troponin, cholesterol), and extreme values are under-predicted,\nwhich an MSE loss encourages.</li>\n<li>Hi-Patch, the planned core model, has no result of its own; the VAE notebook's model, <code>HiPatchVAE</code>, uses a\nHi-Patch-style patch encoder. The learnable-graph model has figures in <code>Reports/luca_results/</code> but no\nnumbers in the report. There is no final report in the repository.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"team\">Team</h2>\n<p>Asal Roudbari, Luca Gianantonio, Saahil Sanganeriya and Nawal Reza. Who built what comes from the contribution line in\nthe midterm report (<a href=\"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts/blob/main/Reports/midterm.tex\"><code>Reports/midterm.tex</code></a>, line 49) and the commit history:</p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Person</th>\n<th>Models in the report</th>\n<th>In this repository</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Asal Roudbari</td>\n<td>Latent ODE, WaveGNN, Hi-Patch</td>\n<td>WaveGNN figures in <code>Reports/Asal-results/</code>; no WaveGNN or Latent ODE code is committed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Luca Gianantonio</td>\n<td>SeFT, KAFNet, learnable graphs</td>\n<td><code>src/models/seft/</code>, <code>src/models/kafnet/</code>, <code>src/models/learnable_graphs/</code>; figures in <code>Reports/luca_results/</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Nawal Reza</td>\n<td>GRU-D, T-PatchGNN, generative VAE</td>\n<td>the three notebooks in <code>src/models/</code>; figures in <code>results/gru-d/</code>, <code>results/t-patch/</code>, <code>Reports/nawal_results/</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Saahil Sanganeriya</td>\n<td>data preprocessing, RainDrop, evaluation</td>\n<td>listed below</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<p>Saahil's part, from his commits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The shared data pipeline: download PhysioNet 2012, parse it, split it, normalise it with training-set statistics only,\nand build one observation graph per patient (<code>scripts/preprocess_data.py</code>, <code>src/preprocess/</code>,\n<code>docs/DATA_PREPROCESSING.md</code>).</li>\n<li>The exploratory analysis (<code>eda_analysis.py</code>, <code>EDA_SUMMARY.md</code>, <code>eda_results/</code>) and the shared metrics\n(<code>src/utils/metrics.py</code>).</li>\n<li>RainDrop adapted from classification to forecasting, then trained and evaluated (<code>src/models/raindrop/</code>,\n<code>results/raindrop/</code>). The changes to the official code are listed in\n<a href=\"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts/blob/main/src/models/raindrop/raindrop_readme.md\"><code>src/models/raindrop/raindrop_readme.md</code></a>.</li>\n<li>The set-up scripts (<code>environment.yml</code>, <code>install_pytorch.py</code>, <code>test_setup.py</code>, <code>test_raindrop_training.py</code>) and\nmerging everyone's results into the midterm report.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"data-preparation\">Data preparation</h2>\n<p><code>scripts/preprocess_data.py</code> runs the pipeline in <code>src/preprocess/preprocessing.py</code>:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Downloads sets A, B and C of the challenge from physionet.org into <code>data/physionet/</code>.</li>\n<li>Parses each stay, converts times to hours and scales them to [0, 1] over the 48 hours, and builds a mask of which\nvalues were measured.</li>\n<li>Removes only NaN and infinite values. Outliers stay (heart rate 300, glucose 800), treated as real critical values,\nnot errors.</li>\n<li>Splits patients 60/20/20 with seed 42 and z-scores every variable with training-set statistics.</li>\n<li>Builds an observation graph per patient and saves everything to <code>data/physionet/processed/</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>In an observation graph each node is one measurement (heart rate at 10:00, for example). Edges join the same variable\nmeasured up to 2 hours apart, different variables measured at the same time step, and each node to itself. The\nmidterm report gives about 150 nodes and 500 edges per patient. Details:\n<a href=\"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts/blob/main/docs/DATA_PREPROCESSING.md\"><code>docs/DATA_PREPROCESSING.md</code></a>.</p>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"how-to-run\">How to run</h2>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\"><pre>conda env create -f environment.yml\nconda activate graphml-imts\npython install_pytorch.py           <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> PyTorch 2.0 and PyTorch Geometric: CUDA, Apple MPS or CPU build</span>\npython scripts/preprocess_data.py   <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> download and preprocess into data/physionet/processed/</span>\npython test_setup.py                <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> check the processed files and load the dataset classes</span></pre></div>\n<p>RainDrop:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\"><pre>python test_raindrop_training.py                                    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> short run to check the pipeline</span>\npython src/models/raindrop/train_raindrop_forecasting.py --epochs 50\npython src/models/raindrop/evaluate_raindrop.py --checkpoint results/raindrop/best_model.pt</pre></div>\n<p>The GRU-D, T-PatchGNN and VAE notebooks were run on Google Colab. Their first two cells mount Google Drive and change\ninto a project folder; they then load <code>processed/{train,val,test}.pt</code>. To run them elsewhere, skip the Drive cell and\nchange into <code>data/physionet/</code> instead.</p>\n<p>The KAFNet, SeFT and learnable-graph scripts (<code>src/models/&lt;name&gt;/train.py</code>) import <code>datasets.dataset</code>\n(<code>PhysioNetDataset</code>, <code>split_history_forecast</code>), a module that was not committed, so they need it before they run.</p>\n<p>To use the processed data in another model:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-python notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\"><pre><span class=\"pl-k\">import</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">sys</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">sys</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">path</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">insert</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\">\"src\"</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-k\">from</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">preprocess</span>.<span class=\"pl-s1\">dataset</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">import</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">PhysioNetDataset</span>, <span class=\"pl-v\">PhysioNetGraphDataset</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">dataset</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">PhysioNetDataset</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\">\"data/physionet/processed\"</span>, <span class=\"pl-s1\">split</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span><span class=\"pl-s\">\"train\"</span>)\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">sample</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">dataset</span>[<span class=\"pl-c1\">0</span>]\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">sample</span>[<span class=\"pl-s\">\"timestamps\"</span>]  <span class=\"pl-c\"># (T,) scaled to [0, 1] over 48 hours</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">sample</span>[<span class=\"pl-s\">\"values\"</span>]      <span class=\"pl-c\"># (T, 41) z-scored; columns 0-4 static, 5-40 the 36 time series</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">sample</span>[<span class=\"pl-s\">\"mask\"</span>]        <span class=\"pl-c\"># (T, 41) 1 = measured, 0 = missing</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-s1\">graphs</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">PhysioNetGraphDataset</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\">\"data/physionet/processed\"</span>, <span class=\"pl-s1\">split</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span><span class=\"pl-s\">\"train\"</span>)  <span class=\"pl-c\"># loads the saved graphs</span></pre></div>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"repository-layout\">Repository layout</h2>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code>scripts/preprocess_data.py      preprocessing entry point\nsrc/preprocess/                 download, parse, split, normalise, build graphs; dataset classes\nsrc/utils/metrics.py            shared metrics\nsrc/models/raindrop/            RainDrop forecasting: train, evaluate, notes; Raindrop/ is the upstream code\nsrc/models/seft/, kafnet/, learnable_graphs/\nsrc/models/*.ipynb              GRU-D, T-PatchGNN and VAE notebooks\neda_analysis.py, eda_results/   exploratory analysis and its figures (summary in EDA_SUMMARY.md)\nresults/                        RainDrop, GRU-D and T-PatchGNN outputs (figures, metrics)\nReports/                        proposal and midterm reports (LaTeX) with their figures\ndocs/DATA_PREPROCESSING.md      preprocessing and graph details\n</code></pre></div>\n<h2 data-anchor=\"credits\">Credits</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>RainDrop: Zhang et al., \"Graph-Guided Network for Irregularly Sampled Multivariate Time Series\", ICLR 2022. The\nofficial code (<a href=\"https://github.com/mims-harvard/Raindrop\">mims-harvard/Raindrop</a>, MIT licence, kept in\n<code>src/models/raindrop/Raindrop/LICENSE</code>) is included with the forecasting changes; the paper's LaTeX source is in\n<code>src/models/raindrop/paper/</code>.</li>\n<li>Data: Silva et al., \"Predicting In-Hospital Mortality of ICU Patients: The PhysioNet/Computing in Cardiology\nChallenge 2012\". References for the other models are in <a href=\"https://github.com/saahilsanganeriya/GraphML-imts/blob/main/Reports/references.bib\"><code>Reports/references.bib</code></a>.</li>\n</ul>"},"tree":{"truncated":false,"withheld":0,"entries":[[".gitignore","b",480],["EDA_SUMMARY.md"